Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-10-2000||11:36 AM||||I know there are many reply's on engine swaps and what not that fiero owners can do. I have a 85SE 4cyl. manual, can anybody tell me what engines i could swap with this...i only want to go up to a V6, or i can stay with a L4, doesn't matter...so what engines can i do (4cyl's and V6's)?<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-10-2000||11:47 AM||||With enough $ you can put any engine in your Fiero.  Replace with another 2.5, a Quad 4, a stock 2.8, bored 2.8 to a  3.1, 3.2, 3.4, crate 3.4, 3.8 series II, a 3.8 s/c. You can hop up any of the V-6's the way you want to. V-8 Archie any V-8  engine.  You'll need to decide on your wallet size and what you want in your car. Kick Hill Farms has engines galore in his barn.||||reg||3
Z||000002||baldlobo||11-10-2000||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>With enough $ you can put any engine in your Fiero.  Replace with another 2.5, a Quad 4, a stock 2.8, bored 2.8 to a  3.1, 3.2, 3.4, crate 3.4, 3.8 series II, a 3.8 s/c. You can hop up any of the V-6's the way you want to. V-8 Archie any V-8  engine.  You'll need to decide on your wallet size and what you want in your car. Kick Hill Farms has engines galore in his barn.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>you forgot one the SuperDuty 4.||||reg||1
